& [Delineation]
  + READY stopped owns a nonterminal handle and legal ADVANCE reentry
  + terminal pending owns an immutable terminal record and one legal reflection-response admission
  + complete owns terminal evidence plus an admitted final semantic output
  + provider absence at pending is expected staged incompleteness and not provider-protocol failure
  + reflection admission changes the orchestration report but never advances or alters terminal procedure state

& [SelectedForms]
  + keep IterativeReport complete and stopped invariants unchanged
  + use TerminalReflectionPendingReport for the third orchestration identity
  + ScriptedTerminalPendingRun retains exact terminal registry and deterministic reflection request but no response or final output
  + completion accepts one supplied reflection envelope and returns the existing ScriptedCompleteRun form
  + validate terminal registry through exact nonmutating INSPECT and READ before pending export and again before response admission

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty distinguishes missing expected reflection from a protocol fault and from complete output
  + Security binds response admission to the entire validated pending wrapper and exact terminal registry
  + Planner reserves exactly one provider call for reflection while exposing no further tool call
  + Weaver reconstructs the advance transcript and deterministic reflection request
  + Scribe retains terminal public evidence request and sanitized admitted response only at completion
  + Refiner keeps exact record and registry outside the model-facing request
  + Observer admits pending and completion only when phase usage projection record and registry agree

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated terminal_pending forms runner validator response-admission helper fixtures and focused tests
  + retain provider transport process clock persistence and all external effects under separate locks

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior or stored data
